// expect: 42
// BANKED RED (unregistered — Hβ.effects.negative-stance-under-mixed-gate).
// A fn whose callee is a MUTUALLY-RECURSIVE `!E`-declaring fn cannot
// declare a closed positive row: `outer` here declares `Cast + !Mutate`
// and proves `Cast(Int) + !Mutate`, and the gate refuses it —
// E_EffectMismatch at outer's own decl span, on every path (check,
// compile, and the concatenated blob alike).
//
// The trigger was isolated by probe, three theories dead first:
//   · bare-declared vs instance-proven ALONE passes (`with Cast` over
//     `addr(x)` — eff_name_handle shares the handle between ENamed and
//     EParameterized, so by-name membership already admits an instance);
//   · negation-beside-positives alone passes (`with Cast + !Mutate`);
//   · a NON-recursive `!Mutate` callee passes.
// Mutual recursion is the discriminator, and the root is named:
// row_without_self (effects.mn) takes the least solution of a recursive
// row equation — "a tail landing on the fn's OWN row handle cuts to the
// closed head" — and that cut is SELF-only. Here the tail lands on a
// CO-MEMBER's handle, so R_ping = names ∪ R_pong and R_pong = names ∪
// R_ping never cut, the row never closes, and the widened tail flows
// into every caller until a closed gate refuses it.
//
// That group-wide cut was REFUTED (2026-07-31, the source dig): a wider
// cut freezes MORE rows — the cut is the defect, not its scope. The
// dissolution is rung 3's edge-set tails: R ∪ R = R, the visiting-set
// read closes every cycle with NO cut (the refuter's hand-trace
// predicts this fixture green under it). A D9 banked gate; it goes
// green when the swap lands, and building any cut from this comment
// is the condemned-forms clause violated.
import runtime/memory

fn ping(n) with !Mutate = if n <= 0 { 0 } else { pong(n - 1) }

fn pong(n) with !Mutate = if n <= 0 { 1 } else { ping(n - 1) }

fn outer(x) with Cast + !Mutate = addr(ping(x))

fn main() = if outer(3) > 0 { 42 } else { 1 }
